My Muscle Map / Strict muscle artwork

This application includes anatomical path data adapted from
src/data/muscles.front.ts and src/data/muscles.back.ts at that revision.
The upstream LICENSE and NOTICE files in this directory are unmodified copies.

Changes made in this application:
- The path strings were converted from TypeScript into Kotlin records used by Jetpack Compose.
- The compound paths serratus-anterior-left, serratus-anterior-right, obliques-left, and obliques-right were split into separate regions. Where a later subpath began with a relative move, that move was rewritten as an absolute move so the separated contour stays in the same place. The vertices of those regions are the upstream vertices.
- shoulder-side-left and shoulder-side-right retain the upstream geometry and also include geometry added locally while adapting that artwork for this application's muscle-region model.
- shoulder-front-left and shoulder-front-right use locally modified and reworked geometry, derived while adapting the upstream artwork for that same muscle-region model.
- Those shoulder modifications were created as part of our own adaptation of the Apache-2.0 body-muscles artwork. They were not copied from another third-party artwork or asset.
- The shoulder geometry is still expected to receive further visual refinement before public release.
